  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 225 PM EDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\n500mb ridging in the region will only be occasionally interrupted by \nweak shortwaves over the region, including tonight/Friday. These \nwill bring some periods of higher clouds, but meager if any precip \nchances. \n\nAn increase in higher clouds tonight should decrease the chances for \nboth fog and frost somewhat heading into Friday morning. Do still \nexpect patchy fog again tonight, in particular in ne lower MI,\nwhere higher clouds will take longer to arrive. Fog is expected\nto be an issue again Fri night.\n\nOtherwise. high pressure over eastern Canada and then the central \nGreat Lakes will keep our wx quiet. Lack of precip requires us to \nkeep an eye on fire wx parameters, but an actually breezy day looks \nto be unlikely until perhaps Tuesday. Daytime RH values are also \nunlikely to completely crater.\n\nOur next decent chance for precip looks to arrive in the middle part \nof next week. Our upper pattern finally tries to become a bit more \nprogressive, allowing an upper trof and surface cold front to slide \neast into the area. This is looking less impressive than yesterday, \nwith a lot of energy/moisture still associated with a stalled upper \nlow in the sw states. Even so, rain chances look to arrive \nhere Tuesday night/Wednesday.",
